/*
Exact constant-body-rate quaternion propagation
Contract
Normalize q, propagate the inertial-to-body quaternion by the exact left-multiplied body-rate increment, normalize the result, and canonicalize w>=0. dt is finite and nonnegative.

Failure handling
Any null pointer -> ADCS_E_NULL. Nonfinite rate/time or negative dt -> ADCS_E_RANGE. Degenerate quaternion -> ADCS_E_DEGENERATE. If out exists, every failure writes identity.

Normative mathematical definition
Let `q_hat=normalize(q)`, `theta=||w||*dt`, and, for nonzero rate,
`dq=[cos(theta/2), sin(theta/2)*w/||w||]`. The required propagation is
`out=canonicalize(normalize(dq tensor-product q_hat))`; the multiplication order and half-angle are mandatory. Your generation must end with this function's closing brace `}`; the harness appends none of its own.
*/
/* Public GNC API and evaluator-local implementation context. */
