/*
Reaction-wheel cluster angular momentum

Operational context
A momentum manager reconstructs total stored momentum for an arbitrary non-orthogonal wheel cluster.

Input interface
wheels: array of count 1..16. Each axis_body is finite and nonzero, inertia_kg_m2 is finite >0, and speed_rad_s finite. momentum output.

Mathematical definition
For wheel k, normalize its supplied body-axis direction a_k and compute h_k=J_k omega_k a_k.
Total body momentum is the vector sum of all h_k. Signed wheel speed determines direction.

Required processing
